OL,2,W//%*// //%Q,. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAEngland's Victorian connection to
OL,4,Athe Bayeux Tapestry
OL,5,
OL,6,FAmong them is the fact penises shown on
OL,7,Fthe original were not stitched on to
OL,8,Fthe 19th Century copy, a decision
OL,9,Fdriven by Victorian prudishness.
OL,11,FWork on the Leek version was led by
OL,12,Fembroiderer Elizabeth Wardle who felt
OL,13,FEngland should have a copy of its own
OL,14,Fafter a visit to Bayeux in France in
OL,15,F1885 to see the original.
